{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the boys grew.</b> This one went to synagogues and houses of study, and this one to houses of idol worship. And thus our Rabbis of blessed memory said: Rebecca would pass by synagogues and houses of study and Jacob would kick to go out, as it is said (Jeremiah 1:5): ״בטרם אצרך בבטן ידעתיך״; she would pass by the doors of idol worship and Esau would kick to go out, as it is said (Psalms 58:4): ״זורו רשעים מרחם״." "<b>And Esau became a man knowing hunting, a man of the field, and Jacob was a plain man, dwelling in tents.</b> Scripture intends to say that even though these brothers were twins formed in the womb at one time, their deeds are not alike, but they are two opposites and all their traits are divided one from the other. For Esau was drawn after the pleasures of the body and Jacob was drawn after the counsel of the soul, and therefore it says 'Esau became a man knowing hunting' — and this is the craft of an idler, one who pursues the desires of the world, 'a man of the field,' as if to say a man of the earth. And from this his name was called Edom, derived from אדום and from אדמה, meaning that he was earthy." "<b>And it is known</b> that a person's exertion in food and drink and his amusement in hunting, which are the pleasures of the body in this world — is it not a cause to despise the service of the Blessed Name and His fear, making them secondary and the pleasures of the body primary? And this was the trait of Esau, as it says: 'and he did eat and drink, and rose up and went his way; and Esau despised the birthright.' And one possessed of this trait finds himself deception (עקוב) in the end, as it says: 'Is not he rightly named Jacob? for he hath supplanted me (ויעקבני) these two times: he took away my birthright; and behold, now he hath taken away my blessing.' And if he tastes honey and sweetness in pleasures, it is only for a moment, and he is destined to worry and be comfortless in his end and to grieve greatly over this, as it is written: 'and he cried with a great and bitter cry.' And so Solomon peace be upon him mentioned, regarding the pursuit of pleasures (Proverbs 5:3–4): ״נופת תטופנה שפתי זרה וגו׳ ואחריתה מרה כלענה״. This is the way of Esau and all who support his steps, but the way and trait of Jacob is the opposite of this, for 'a plain man' is the opposite of 'knowing hunting,' and 'dwelling in tents' is the opposite of 'a man of the field.' And furthermore, what Esau wished to acquire, Jacob wished to sell — and that is the pursuit of desires and the seeking of worldly pleasures, which he likened to a lentil stew, because the good of the world and its tranquility and its honor is nothing but a circle like a lentil, which is round. And therefore he wished to sell and to exchange transient life for the life of the world, which is the service of the Blessed Name that was in the birthright." "<b>And know</b> that from the fact that Scripture mentioned concerning each of them 'a man' (איש), we learn that each of them was not under thirteen (י״ג) years of age. But according to the reckoning of the years of Abraham you will find that at the time he sold him the birthright each was fifteen (ט״ו) years old, for Abraham was a hundred years old when Isaac was born, and he was a hundred and forty (ק״מ) when Isaac married Rebecca, and twenty years of barrenness — that makes a hundred and sixty (ק״ס) years for Abraham; and all his years were one hundred and seventy-five (קע״ה). Accordingly, on the day Abraham died, Jacob and Esau were fifteen (ט״ו) years old." "<b>And furthermore,</b> the passage alludes to us that Gehenna is prepared for the faction of Esau and the Garden of Eden is prepared for the faction of Jacob and his sons. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: that when these two brothers came before their father to receive the blessings, the one entered with the Garden of Eden and the other with Gehenna — the Garden of Eden entered with Jacob and Gehenna entered with Esau, as will be explained for each in its place. And likewise they expounded: ״היא העולה״ — this is the Edomite nation, which exalts itself, as it is said (Obadiah 4): ״אם תגביה כנשר וגו׳״; ״על מוקדה״ — this is Gehenna in the world to come; and in this world — ״והיבת ליקידת אשא״." "<b>And Jacob was a whole-hearted man.</b> It should have said ויעקב היה איש תם, just as it said ויהי עשו, and likewise Scripture said (Genesis 4:2): ״ויהי הבל רועה צאן וקין היה עובד אדמה״. But it mentioned the term הויה for Esau because so was his name always, from the day he was born it never changed at all; whereas the name of Jacob was changed afterward to the name Israel. Therefore it did not use the term הויה for him, because the essential הויה is not in the name Jacob but in the name Israel, as HaShem, blessed be He, said to him (Genesis 35:10): ״כי אם ישראל יהיה שמך״." "<b>And further,</b> you should reflect that it should have said 'Jacob, a man of truth (אמת),' since his attribute is truth, as the prophet said (Micah 7:20): ״תתן אמת ליעקב״. But He explained with the word תם, which alludes to the attribute of truth, and further alludes that he is the decisive one, from the term תיומת, which is the middle line between the right and the left. And you already know that the numerical value of יעקב with the four letters is קו״ף, and R. Akiva said: קו״ף — this is the Holy One, blessed be He. And understand this." "<b>Dwelling in tents.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): of Shem and Eber, and concerning this it says יושב אהלים." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: יושב אהלים — the tent above and the tent below. For you already know that the image of Jacob is engraved upon the Throne of Glory, and behold, this is as if it said: יושב כסא."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {3 "Comment [3] cites two ages for the twins at the sale of the birthright (י״ג in the first sentence, then ט״ו); translated exactly as written.", 4 "The closing Aramaic phrase והיבת ליקידת אשא is from the Targum of Leviticus 1:17 ('it is an offering made by fire'); preserved in Aramaic as in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:27.071036086Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}